  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "The value of \\(20\\) quarters and \\(10\\) dimes equals the value of \\(10\\) quarters and \\(n\\) dimes. What is \\(n?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\)",
    "B": "\\(20\\)",
    "C": "\\(30\\)",
    "D": "\\(35\\)",
    "E": "\\(45\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Remove \\(10\\) quarters from each collection. The remaining \\(n\\) dimes must have the same value as \\(10\\) quarters and \\(10\\) dimes.\n\nA quarter is worth \\(25\\) cents and a dime is worth \\(10\\) cents, so that remaining value is\n\\[\n10\\cdot25+10\\cdot10=350\\text{ cents}.\n\\]\nThe number of dimes needed is therefore\n\\[\nn=350\\div10=35.\n\\]\nThus \\(n=35\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
